    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gythēum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gythī^um</span></b> , i, n., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γύθειον</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γύθιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a seaport in Laconia</i>, <i>on the
				Eurotas</i>, now <i>Paleopoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 34,
				39, § 214</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				3, 11, 49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 34, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 27</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gythĕātes</span></b> , ae,
			m., adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γυθεάτης</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Gythēum</i>, <i>Gytheatic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pontus, Mela, 2, 3, 9: sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 5, 8, § 16</span></i>
			. </div>
